OFFICE OF THE KAZEKAGE -- REFORMS OF THE FIFTH KAZEKAGE ERA

Under Lord Gaara, Fifth Kazekage and host of the One-Tail, Sunagakure has
turned from an age of fear toward one of trust. These are the standing reforms
of his administration.

1. Alliance foremost -- The bond with Konohagakure is affirmed as the
   cornerstone of the village's security. Cooperative missions and shared
   intelligence are encouraged, not merely permitted.
2. Care for the shinobi -- Genin welfare, water rationing fairness, and the
   treatment of the wounded are elevated priorities. The Kazekage personally
   reviews hardship petitions.
3. Rehabilitation of the jinchuriki's example -- Where past hosts were isolated
   and weaponized, the office now models the jinchuriki as protector of the
   village, not its living arsenal.
4. Open academy -- Recruitment broadened; the Kazekage speaks to new genin
   directly to instill purpose over fear.

Lord Gaara governs by the creed that a Kage protects the village with his own
person. These reforms are to be upheld by all division heads.
